@id("close-workorder-main-with-person-approval")
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"MaintData___close_workorder", resource)
when { context.input.site_id == "MAIN" }
when temporal {
  formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Yarbeck___get_approval"::response{
    eventResource: resource,
    input.site_id: context.input.site_id,
    input.wonum: context.input.wonum,
    output.decision: Drupe::decision::"ACCEPTED",
    output.approver_kind: Drupe::approver_kind::"PERSON"
  }
};

// The approval lookup must itself be permitted, otherwise it is never recorded as a response.
@id("allow-yarbeck-approval-lookup")
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"Yarbeck___get_approval", resource);

// Other read-only lookups only. No approve, assign, cancel, generate or update is permitted.
@id("allow-read-only-lookups")
permit (principal, action in [
  Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_workorder",
  Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_workorder_tasks",
  Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_workorder_costs",
  Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_workorder_actuals_vs_planned",
  Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_workorder_kpis",
  Drupe::Action::"MaintData___list_workorders",
  Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_my_assigned_workorders",
  Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_schedule_calendar",
  Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_failure_codes",
  Drupe::Action::"Vantry___get_yarbeck_approval"
], resource);
```

I treated only `Yarbeck___get_approval` as proof of approval, because approvals are decided and recorded in Yarbeck. `Vantry___get_yarbeck_approval` is allowed as a read-only lookup but does not unlock closing.

`MaintData___approve_workorder` has no permit, so the agent cannot approve work orders and is denied by default. The same applies to every other write tool except closing.

The close permit requires all of these:
- The site is `MAIN`.
- A completed Yarbeck lookup (a recorded `::response`, so failed or denied calls don't count) from the last hour matches the same `wonum` and `site_id`.
- That lookup returned `ACCEPTED` and the approver kind `PERSON`. `REFUSED`, `OPEN`, `AUTOMATION` and `SERVICE` don't qualify.

